":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":8,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've made the change to PKT-0068 and committed it as `9f5f8e1`. Both acceptance commands pass: the unit oracle shows 178 passed and 1 skipped, and lint has 0 errors (its one warning is in AdminPanel, unrelated). I could not run the before/after latency measurement the goal asks for. Nothing was listening on :8080 and there is no docker daemon here, so `.theseus/oracle/perf/e2e-convert.js` had no stack to measure against.\n\n**What changed**\n- **`DocService/sources/converterservice.js`:** synchronous conversions now check the task status first after 50 ms, then wait twice as long each time, up to the old 1000 ms.\n- **Timeout:** each wait is added to the total, so a conversion still gets `CONVERT_TIMEOUT` once the total wait is strictly over the limit, as before.\n- **`tests/unit/converterService.tests.js`:** only the expected sleep sequences changed, plus one test title and one comment to match:\n  - `[1000]` became `[50]` (two tests).\n  - `[1000, 1000, 1000]` became `[50, 100, 200]`.\n  - The timeout test went from four 1000s to `[50, 100, 200, 400, 800, 1000, 1000]`. With the 3000 ms limit, the total reaches 2550 after six waits and 3550 after the seventh, which triggers the timeout.\n\n**Decisions**\n- I took the shape of the change from PKT-0063's Executor log, which also had a 50 ms floor and kept the timeout semantics.\n- Without a measurement, the expected gain is an estimate: a conversion that finishes in under a second should now return after about 50–350 ms instead of 1000 ms. The cost is up to about 6 extra database status checks in the first 1.5 s of each sync request.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas**\n- `converterService.tests.js` asserts the exact sleep sequence, so any change to sync polling timing must list that test file in `target`.\n- A packet that asks for an end-to-end perf measurement should declare it needs a running stack with `requires:`, because the executor environment may not have one.\n\nThe Executor log, the Atlas lessons and the friction line are written and committed. `theseus validate` reports 0 errors and 1 warning. I didn't look at what the warning is.","ttft_ms":1763,"type":"result","duration_ms":47216,"uuid":"4c43b0af-a2f7-4866-a920-1f720e3ea912","ttft_stream_ms":944,"time_to_request_ms":384,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":230,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":24,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":7,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":7,"init_frame_send":6,"engine_pickup":6,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":2,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":11,"query_setup":6,"auto_mode_context_wait":33,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":25,"message_normalization":1,"client_creation":3,"request_build":6},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":110,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":258,"time_to_request_major_faults":1,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":216,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":140,"process_rss_mib_result":223,"process_anon_mib_result":132,"process_peak_rss_mib":229,"process_cpu_ms_turn":1960,"process_wall_ms_turn":47216,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":623,"process_wall_ms_streaming":18809,"main_stream_count":8,"main_stream_event_count":539,"main_stream_chunk_count":322,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":9,"cpu_ms":20,"major_faults":0,"setup_ms":0,"prompt_producers_ms":0,"ambient_start_ms":12,"ambient_wait_ms":8,"render_ms":1,"producers":41,"token_counts":0},"first_content_frame_ms":944,"time_to_request_from_spawn_ms":20619614,"warm_spare_claimed":false,"flag_fetch_kick":"started_in_init_warm","time_origin_ms":1793656075906.184,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"process_start_tuning":0}
